          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On Wednesday, June 30, 2010, around 5:15 PM, a witness is intrigued by the presence of a large black dot stationary in the sky. This dot then moves and disappears behind a cloud. Of average strangeness and good consistency despite a lack of orientation, this observation of a large black dot cannot be concluded at this time; further checks on various hypotheses cannot be made. Unfortunately, the one-month delay after which the questionnaire arrived does not allow for obtaining radar records. This case is classified C due to lack of independent testimonies and cross-references.",
